Description: XDJ-style behavior tweaks (waveform EQ decoupling, loop from cue)
 1. The RGB waveform shows the track's frequency content like on Pioneer
    hardware: the EQ knobs and kill switches no longer scale the waveform
    bands, so a closed EQ still shows whether the track has bass/mid/high
    at that point. The per-band visual gains from the waveform preferences
    still apply.
 2. Pressing loop-out with no loop-in set creates a loop starting at the
    main cue point (Pioneer behavior), instead of being ignored.
Author: Pioneered CI <pioneered-build@localhost>
Forwarded: no

